{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>He gathers them all with a hook</b> — like מכמורת (a fish-spear)." "<b>He drags him</b> — he gathers him, like: יתגוררו יסורו בי (let them be gathered, let them turn to me)." "<b>And his net</b> — like רשתו משטח חרמים (his net, a spreading of nets)." "<b>Therefore he rejoices</b> — that he takes everything without effort. Or חרמו (his net) is a designation for his idol."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:58.141498363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}